                            <comment id="15978364" author="1ambda" created="Fri, 21 Apr 2017 09:12:28 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Linked to &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-2440&quot; title=&quot;[Umbrella] Platform Compatibility Issues&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-2440&quot;&gt;ZEPPELIN-2440&lt;/a&gt; (platform compatibility issue)&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15979091" author="githubbot" created="Fri, 21 Apr 2017 17:18:27 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;GitHub user cfries opened a pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/2276&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/2276&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-2410&quot; title=&quot; (Windows) Helium.java fails to create HeliumOnlineRegistry&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-2410&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-2410&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Using UUID from filename in registry cache dir inste&#8230;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &#8230;ad of uri.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    The previous version of this file used the full uri as file name in the&lt;br/&gt;
    cache. This included special characters like the : in http: which&lt;br/&gt;
    caused problems.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Since this is just a cache file, a better approach is to use an UUID.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    The UUID is constructed from the URI to avoid the cache dir to grow&lt;br/&gt;
    over time (in case there is no clean up of the cache dir).&lt;/p&gt;

