&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;commit 5fda58f29c261b8fd61353a2b09c0f90c19d3fa4&lt;br/&gt;
Author: Christian Fries &amp;lt;email@christian-fries.de&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Date:   2017-04-21T15:07:00Z&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-2410&quot; title=&quot; (Windows) Helium.java fails to create HeliumOnlineRegistry&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-2410&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-2410&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Using UUID from filename in registry cache dir instead of uri.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    The previous version of this file used the full uri as file name in the&lt;br/&gt;
    cache. This included special characters like the : in http: which&lt;br/&gt;
    caused problems.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Since this is just a cache file, a better approach is to use an UUID.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    The UUID is constructed from the URI to avoid the cache dir to grow&lt;br/&gt;
    over time (in case there is no clean up of the cache dir).&lt;/p&gt;

